%C3%A2tre_du_Ch%C3%A2telet\" title=\"Théâtre du Châtelet\">Théâtre du Châtelet</a>, Paris</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\">Genre</th><td class=\"infobox-data category hlist\"><a href=\"/wiki/Vocal_jazz\" title=\"Vocal jazz\">Vocal jazz</a></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\">Length</th><td class=\"infobox-data\"><span class=\"duration\"><span class=\"min\">91</span>:<span class=\"s\">09</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\">Label</th><td class=\"infobox-data hlist\"><a href=\"/wiki/Justin_Time_Records\" title=\"Justin Time Records\">Justin Time</a></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><i><b>In the City of Lights</b></i> is the title of a live concert date by American jazz diva <a href=\"/wiki/Sarah_Vaughan\" title=\"Sarah Vaughan\">Sarah Vaughan</a>, performing at the <a href=\"/wiki/Th%C3%A9%C3%A2tre_du_Ch%C3%A2telet\" title=\"Théâtre du Châtelet\">Théâtre du Châtelet</a> in Paris.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-AllmusicReview&#95;1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-AllmusicReview-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>   Recorded in 1985, the album was not released until 1999, almost a decade after Vaughan's death in 1990.\n</p>\n<meta property=\"mw:PageProp/toc\" />\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Reception\">Reception</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=In_the_City_of_Lights&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Reception\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<table class=\"wikitable floatright\" style=\"width:24.2em;font-size:88%;text-align:center;margin:0.5em 0 0.5em 1em;padding:0;border-spacing:0\"><caption style=\"font-size:115%\">Professional ratings</caption><tbody><tr><th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;color:#202122;background:#d1dbdf;font-size:100%\">Review scores</th></tr><tr><th scope=\"col\">Source</th><th scope=\"col\">Rating</th></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align:center;vertical-align:middle\"><i><a href=\"/wiki/Allmusic\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Allmusic\">Allmusic</a></i></td><td style=\"text-align:center;vertical-align:middle\"><span style=\"white-space:nowrap\" title=\"4/5 stars\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span title=\"4/5 stars\"><img alt=\"Star\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Star_full.svg/20px-Star_full.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Star_full.svg/40px-Star_full.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"108\" data-file-height=\"110\" /></span></span><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"Star\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Star_full.svg/20px-Star_full.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Star_full.svg/40px-Star_full.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"108\" data-file-height=\"110\" /></span></span><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"Star\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Star_full.svg/20px-Star_full.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Star_full.svg/40px-Star_full.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"108\" data-file-height=\"110\" /></span></span><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"Star\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Star_full.svg/20px-Star_full.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Star_full.svg/40px-Star_full.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"108\" data-file-height=\"110\" /></span></span><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Star_empty.svg/20px-Star_empty.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Star_empty.svg/40px-Star_empty.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"108\" data-file-height=\"110\" /></span></span></span><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-AllmusicReview&#95;1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-AllmusicReview-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/Allmusic\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Allmusic\">Allmusic</a> review by Dave Nathan said: \"Probably more than any of her contemporaries with whom she is most often compared, Sarah Vaughan's voice not only survived the vicissitudes of years of performing, but matured remarkably well. Her performance at this concert assured all that she could still go from bluesy growls through crystal clarity to sounding cute at the higher range...Vaughan makes a dramatic entrance singing \"Summertime\" a capella, establishing the vocal framework for the remainder of the concert. Vaughan is fully aware that her voice and persona are special. She is not all reluctant to use them to milk that last droplet of applause from the audience....The 2,500 plus people who attended the Chetelet concert that evening would not let Vaughan leave the stage.\".<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-AllmusicReview&#95;1-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-AllmusicReview-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Track_listing\">Track listing</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=In_the_City_of_Lights&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Track listing\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<ol><li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/Hi-Fly_(Randy_Weston_song)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Hi-Fly (Randy Weston song)\">Hi-Fly</a>\" (<a href=\"/wiki/Randy_Weston\" title=\"Randy Weston\">Randy Weston</a>) – 8:23 (<a href=\"/wiki/Instrumental\" title=\"Instrumental\">instrumental</a>)</li>\n<li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/Summertime_(George_Gershwin_song)\" title=\"Summertime (George Gershwin song)\">Summertime</a>\" (<a href=\"/wiki/George_Gershwin\" title=\"George Gershwin\">George Gershwin</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/DuBose_Heyward\" title=\"DuBose Heyward\">DuBose Heyward</a>) – 2:36</li>\n<li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/Just_Friends_(1931_song)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Just Friends (1931 song)\">Just Friends</a>\" (<a href=\"/wiki/John_Klenner\" title=\"John Klenner\">John Klenner</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Sam_M._Lewis\" title=\"Sam M. Lewis\">Sam M. Lewis</a>) – 2:31</li>\n<li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/Wave_(Antonio_Carlos_Jobim_song)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Wave (Antonio Carlos Jobim song)\">Wave</a>\" (<a href=\"/wiki/Ant%C3%B4nio_Carlos_Jobim\" title=\"Antônio Carlos Jobim\">Antônio Carlos Jobim</a>) – 8:22</li>\n<li>\"On a Clear Day (You Can See Forever)\" (<a href=\"/wiki/Burton_Lane\" title=\"Burton Lane\">Burton Lane</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Alan_Jay_Lerner\" title=\"Alan Jay Lerner\">Alan Jay Lerner</a>) – 1:58</li>\n<li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/If_You_Could_See_Me_Now_(1946_song)\" title=\"If You Could See Me Now (1946 song)\">If You Could See Me Now</a>\" (<a href=\"/wiki/Tadd_Dameron\" title=\"Tadd Dameron\">Tadd Dameron</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Carl_Sigman\" title=\"Carl Sigman\">Carl Sigman</a>) – 6:22</li>\n<li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/I%27ve_Got_the_World_on_a_String\" title=\"I&#39;ve Got the World on a String\">I've Got the World on a String</a>\" (<a href=\"/wiki/Harold_Arlen\" title=\"Harold Arlen\">Harold Arlen</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Ted_Koehler\" title=\"Ted Koehler\">Ted Koehler</a>) – 3:30</li>\n<li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/Fascinating_Rhythm\" title=\"Fascinating Rhythm\">Fascinating Rhythm</a>\" (G. Gershwin, <a href=\"/wiki/Ira_Gershwin\" title=\"Ira Gershwin\">Ira Gershwin</a>) – 3:35</li>\n<li>Medley: \"<a href=\"/wiki/But_Not_for_Me_(song)\" title=\"But Not for Me (song)\">But Not for Me</a>\"/\"<a href=\"/wiki/Our_Love_Is_Here_to_Stay\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Our Love Is Here to Stay\">Our Love Is Here to Stay</a>\"/\"<a href=\"/wiki/Embraceable_You\" title=\"Embraceable You\">Embraceable You</a>\"/\"<a href=\"/wiki/Someone_to_Watch_over_Me_(song)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Someone to Watch over Me (song)\">Someone to Watch Over Me</a>\" (G. Gershwin, I. Gershwin) – 9:39</li>\n<li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/There_Will_Never_Be_Another_You\" title=\"There Will Never Be Another You\">There Will Never Be Another You</a>\" (<a href=\"/wiki/Mack_Gordon\" title=\"Mack Gordon\">Mack Gordon</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Harry_Warren\" title=\"Harry Warren\">Harry Warren</a>) – 1:32</li>\n<li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/Misty_(song)\" title=\"Misty (song)\">Misty</a>\" (<a href=\"/wiki/Johnny_Burke_(lyricist)\" title=\"Johnny Burke (lyricist)\">Johnny Burke</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Erroll_Garner\" title=\"Erroll Garner\">Erroll Garner</a>) – 6:08</li></ol>\n<p><b>Disc Two</b>\n</p>\n<ol><li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/My_Funny_Valentine\" title=\"My Funny Valentine\">My Funny Valentine</a>\" (<a href=\"/wiki/Lorenz_Hart\" title=\"Lorenz Hart\">Lorenz Hart</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Richard_Rodgers\" title=\"Richard Rodgers\">Richard Rodgers</a>) – 8:31</li>\n<li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/From_This_Moment_On_(Cole_Porter_song)\" title=\"From This Moment On (Cole Porter song)\">From This Moment On</a>\" (<a href=\"/wiki/Cole_Porter\" title=\"Cole Porter\">Cole Porter</a>) – 3:33</li>\n<li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/Send_in_the_Clowns\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Send in the Clowns\">Send in the Clowns</a>\" (<a href=\"/wiki/Stephen_Sondheim\" title=\"Stephen Sondheim\">Stephen Sondheim</a>) – 6:13</li>\n<li>\"Sassy's Blues\" (<a href=\"/wiki/Quincy_Jones\" title=\"Quincy Jones\">Quincy Jones</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Sarah_Vaughan\" title=\"Sarah Vaughan\">Sarah Vaughan</a>) – 4:15</li>\n<li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/Tenderly\" title=\"Tenderly\">Tenderly</a>\" (<a href=\"/wiki/Walter_Gross_(musician)\" title=\"Walter Gross (musician)\">Walter Gross</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Jack_Lawrence_(songwriter)\" title=\"Jack Lawrence (songwriter)\">Jack Lawrence</a>) – 3:49</li>\n<li>\"Scat Chase (Sassy's Blues)\" (Jones, Vaughan) – 6:06</li>\n<li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/Once_in_a_While_(1937_song)\" title=\"Once in a While (1937 song)\">Once in a While</a>\" (<a href=\"/wiki/Michael_Edwards_(American_composer)\" title=\"Michael Edwards (American composer)\">Michael Edwards</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Bud_Green\" title=\"Bud Green\">Bud Green</a>) – 4:09</li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Personnel\">Personnel</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=In_the_City_of_Lights&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Personnel\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Performance\">Performance</h3><span class=\"mw-editse